```

### How to use this in your own code

```python
import requests

url = "https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/ip_addresses/123.123.123.123"
headers = {
    "x-apikey": "elite_api_key_here",
    "Accept": "application/json"
}
params = {
    "limit": 7,
    "cursor": "next_seven"
}

response = requests.get(url, headers=headers, params=params)
data = response.json()
print(data)
```

> **Note:** Replace `"elite_api_key_here"` with your actual elite API key. The `cursor` parameter is optional; if you’re paginating through results, you’ll receive a cursor value in the response that you can pass back in subsequent requests.

If you run the above code against the real VirusTotal API, you’ll get the actual WHOIS descriptors for the IP address, limited to 7 results, and the cursor will be set to whatever the API returns (here shown as `"next_seven"` for illustration).
